# Defect 2175, 2026-10-21, panel 227's R3 (written by its compiler seat): a
# `slice` with nothing to slice is told its count, and the note names the
# call's shape, the value first, as a declared function's note names its
# signature. A built-in with no unlabelled first position takes no note.

function main()
    line = "hello world"
    print(line)
    part = slice(from: 0, to: 5)  #~ wrong_arity
    print(part)
    print(line.len(1))  #~ wrong_arity
